        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "Done and verified end-to-end on c4_sample/ (9,898 files, 800MB).\n\n**What was built in /app:**\n- `pyproject.toml` + uv venv (`.venv`) — only dependency is `zstandard`; `uv sync` installs everything, `uv run` adds nothing.\n- **`/app/compress.py <input_dir> <output_dir>`**: packs all files into zstd-compressed tar chunks (`data/part_NNNN/chunk_NNNNNN.zst`, ≤15MB uncompressed content each, ≤30 files per directory including the `part_*` subdirs), plus a `manifest.json` mapping original relative paths → chunks. Creates the output dir if missing; errors out if any single file exceeds 15MB.\n- **`/app/decompress.py <resharded_dir>`**: reads the manifest, extracts every chunk back to the original paths, then deletes `manifest.json` and `data/` in-place.\n\n**Verification results:**\n- Compress: 9,898 files → 330 chunks in ~8s; no directory exceeds 30 entries; no file exceeds 15MB (compressed size dropped to 297MB).\n- Decompress: `diff -r` against the original reports **IDENTICAL**, with resharding artifacts fully removed.",
